program            = 001_statement_expressions
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = GCC statement expressions in value position including inside macros, folded and volatile-runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
UB-GATE DEVIATION AND ITS REASON. Every program in area 08_gcc_extensions drops
-pedantic from the default warning gate. Reason: the constructs under test are
non-standard GCC extensions by definition, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
them; retaining it would fail every program in the area for doing exactly what it is
meant to do. This is the only area-wide deviation in the corpus. No other warning is
relaxed: -Wall, -Wextra, -Wconversion, -Wsign-conversion, -Wshadow and -Werror are all
retained, and this program is clean under them at -O0, -O1 and -O2. Measured with
gcc 13.3.0.

UB-FREEDOM ARGUMENT. Every value is a small int; no computation approaches INT_MIN or
INT_MAX, so there is no signed overflow. No shift operator is used. No pointer, array or
aggregate is used, so there is no aliasing violation and no one-past-end pointer. Every
object is initialized before it is read, including every statement-expression local. No
object is modified twice between sequence points: the compound assignments inside the
sequencing statement expression are separate full statements. Every printf call receives
at most one side-effecting argument. Nothing depends on padding bytes or on the addresses
of unrelated objects. The for loop in SE_TRIANGLE has a fixed bound and always terminates.
Statement-expression macro locals are uniquely prefixed (mx_, sq_, tr_, and per-use letter
prefixes) and no macro is ever nested inside itself, so -Wshadow is not tripped; the
nesting that does occur, SE_MAX(SE_SQUARE(3), SE_TRIANGLE(4)), combines different macros
with disjoint local names.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is observed, so no target restriction is needed and all
four targets are compared. Only int-typed values are used, so the measured width
differences cannot be reached: sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on
x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64. Plain char is never used, so the measured char-signedness
difference cannot be reached either: char is signed on x86_64 and i686 but unsigned on
aarch64 and riscv64. No address or pointer value is printed. Output is therefore
identical on all four targets at all three optimization levels.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
se_folded_max=12
se_folded_square=81
se_folded_triangle=55
se_folded_nested=10
se_folded_direct=6
se_folded_seq=7
se_folded_arg=5
se_runtime_max=12
se_runtime_square=81
se_runtime_triangle=55
se_runtime_nested=10
se_runtime_direct=6
se_runtime_seq=7
se_runtime_arg=8
END
